{"kind":"assert","text":"Answer to 7454e180: the source has no in-place upgrade, so LC-5 stays at trust rows, packets, test and the 0.6.0 opening, and a small SH head moves the descriptors with the ids you report. The screens need no outage. (1) `install-application` is `step: \"open\"` on \"installation\" (packages/platform/src/application-install.ts:47), so each install opens a new installation item. Its id is the seq the rules scope assigns to the accepted install act (application-install.ts:122-125; the reader takes `state.item(item)` with item ≤ head, application-install-reader.ts:28-31). You learn the id when the install is accepted, not before. (2) Nothing retires the older installation: the rules declare no retire or replace act, and the reader serves any item in state \"active\" (application-install-reader.ts:31). The old item stays active, its row keeps the old presentation, and its release stays trusted, so each screen keeps serving the old item until the SH deployment moves its row. (3) A new install gets a new application scope (application-install.ts:240 sets `scope` to the created scope), so the 0.5.0 installation starts with fresh application state; nothing carries from the 0.4.0 item. The room's membership stays, since the installation refers to the room's membership scope. One rules scope holds at most 16 active definitions (application-install.ts:132). Gate START follows for head 4b606537.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}